.\" kpxcd.8 — Man page for the KeePassXC Daemon
.TH KPXCD 8 "2026-05-18" "kpxcd" "System Manager's Manual"

.SH NAME
kpxcd \- KeePassXC headless daemon for Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpxcd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpxcd
is a headless user-session daemon that keeps one or more KeePass databases unlocked
and available through standard Linux interprocess interfaces. It is designed for
unattended or programmatic access to passwords, SSH keys, and passkeys throughout
a login session, without requiring the KeePassXC GUI to be running.

Upon startup, \fBkpxcd\fR reads its configuration from
\fI~/.config/kpxcd/kpxcd.toml\fR (or the path specified with
\fB\-\-config\fR), loads any databases marked for auto-unlock, and begins
listening on the following interfaces:

.TP
.B D-Bus session bus
Exposes \fBorg.keepassxc.Daemon\fR for management operations and
\fBorg.freedesktop.secrets\fR for Secret Service compatibility.
.TP
.B Unix domain socket (SSH agent)
Listens on \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/ssh.sock\fR and speaks the OpenSSH
agent protocol, allowing \fBssh\fR to use keys stored in the unlocked
databases.
.TP
.B Unix domain socket (control)
Listens on \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/control.sock\fR for local CLI
communication via \fBkpxcctl\fR(1).

All sensitive data (master passwords, derived keys, decrypted entries) is held
in \fBmlock\fR(2)-ed pages and processed within secure memory scopes that zero
registers and stack on return.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Path to the configuration file. Defaults to
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kpxcd/kpxcd.toml\fR, falling back to
\fI~/.config/kpxcd/kpxcd.toml\fR.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
\fBkpxcd\fR is configured via a TOML file. The full reference is in
\fBkpxcd.toml\fR(5). The configuration defines:

.RS
.TP
.B [daemon]
Global settings: idle timeout, screen-lock behavior, log level, SSH mode.
.TP
.B [[database]]
One or more database entries: path, auto-unlock behavior, credential source,
SSH key exposure.
.TP
.B [secret_service]
Secret Service D-Bus settings: enable/disable, notifications, Polkit
confirmation.
.TP
.B [ssh_agent]
SSH agent settings: enable/disable, key lifetime, confirm-on-use.
.TP
.B [fido2]
FIDO2 / passkey settings: AAGUID, supported algorithms, user verification.
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kpxcd/kpxcd.toml
Default configuration file. See \fBkpxcd.toml\fR(5).

.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/ssh.sock
Unix domain socket for the SSH agent protocol. Permissions: 0600.

.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kpxcd/control.sock
Unix domain socket for the control (JSON-RPC) protocol. Permissions: 0600.

.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.keepassxc.daemon.policy
Polkit policy file defining authorization requirements for sensitive operations.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the default configuration directory. If set, the config file is
sought at \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kpxcd/kpxcd.toml\fR.

.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory for runtime files (sockets). Must be set and must be a per-user,
per-session directory. Defaults to \fI/run/user/$UID\fR.

.TP
.B CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY
If set (by systemd \fBLoadCredential=\fR), \fBkpxcd\fR reads auto-unlock
passwords from \fI$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/<credential-name>\fR.

.TP
.B SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Used when \fBssh_mode = "proxy"\fR. \fBkpxcd\fR forwards agent requests to
the socket specified here.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Start the daemon with the default config:
.nf
    kpxcd
.fi

.TP
.B Start with a custom config file:
.nf
    kpxcd --config /etc/kpxcd/my-config.toml
.fi

.TP
.B Run as a systemd user service:
.nf
    systemctl --user enable --now kpxcd.service
.fi

.TP
.B Check if the daemon is running:
.nf
    kpxcctl ping
.fi

.SH BUGS
Report bugs at the project repository.

Known limitations:
.RS
.TP
.B No database write support
\fBkpxcd\fR reads databases but never modifies them. Concurrent writes by
KeePassXC are detected via file watchers, which cause a database re-read.

.TP
.B Cold boot attacks
\fBmlock\fR prevents swap-out but does not prevent DRAM retention attacks.
Use encrypted swap and LUKS for full disk encryption.

.TP
.B Root compromise
\fBkpxcd\fR does not defend against a compromised root account. This is
consistent with the Linux security model.
.RE

.SH AUTHOR
kpxcd was written as a standalone project. It shares no code with KeePassXC.

